ooses, and its weight"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"summed along the path. With floating-point weights the sum can differ from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"diameter(weight:)"},{"type":"text","text":" in the last digit because it adds in a different order. O(n)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/Trees\/Tree\/diameterPath(weight:)","url":"\/documentation\/treealgorithms\/trees\/tree\/diameterpath(weight:)","title":"diameterPath(weight:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://TreeAlgorithms/documentation/TreeAlgorithms/Trees/Tree/centroidDecomposition()":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"centroidDecomposition"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Trees10RootedTreeV","text":"RootedTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The centroid decomposition: the rooted tree on the same vertices whose root is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"centroid (the first in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order when there are two), whose root’s children are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the centroids, chosen the same way, of the components left when it is removed, and so on."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Its edges are not the tree’s: one (parent, child) per vertex but the root, in vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"children(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is in vertex order. Height at most ⌊log₂ n⌋. O(n log n)."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/Trees\/Tree\/centroidDecomposition()","title":"centroidDecomposition()","url":"\/documentation\/treealgori